<title>GREECE: Athens bourse wants revision of share buyback rule.</title>
<headline>Athens bourse wants revision of share buyback rule.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Athens stock exchange has asked the capital market commission to revise presidential decree 14/93 regarding company share buybacks, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The proposed revision aims to simpify bureaucratic procedures involved in 10 percent share buybacks by Athens stock exchange listings.</p>
<p>Under the exchange's proposal, company shareholder assemblies will be allowed to decide on share buybacks as long as they achieve the required quorum for share capital increases and not the presently required 75 percent, the bourse said.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
